The reference keeps one mutable instance inside the builder, each setter mutates it and returns `self`, and `build()` returns it. That satisfies the provided tests but has two weaknesses worth discussing in an interview: there is no validation, and the builder and the product share one object, so a reused builder changes earlier results.

